# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/drafter-bf16 four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/drafter-bf16 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/drafter-bf16 commit; a commit of a file the image carries needs a new
# B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent, and deploys nothing.
# D2: TIMED arm B of the paired ABAB on coding prompts (audits off): B = the bf16 drafter; A = c2-packed-tp4-best-strace, B = c2-packed-tp4-best-dbf16; the pair differs in QWEN_FAST_DRAFTER_BF16 alone (test_tp4_dbf16).
# Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order. Runs only if S1 passed. The tests: warmup, coding (real code), concurrent4 and its steady phase, and
# concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k): the four-user rounds are where the drafter pass lives (one 64-row quad trace per round).
# READ: the committed tokens per round per user are logged by the baked packed audit ('[PACKED] request=... emitted=N', one line per user per round) and the round time by the '[PHASE] execute' stamps. After all
# four arms, offline on each pair's server logs: py -3.11 -B scripts/ci/drafter_bf16.py compare <A server log> <B server log> --live 4 (committed counts per round per user, tau of each arm, median round, per-user tok/s,
# the B/A ratios), and scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (the texts must be identical: exit 0). The drafter's extra weight read is
# about 0.97 ms per pass at 420 GB/s (about 1% of the 100 ms four-user round; scripts/ci/drafter_bf16.py cost), so B wins only if its tau gain exceeds the round-time ratio B/A. Judge PAIRED per round,
# never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run; repeat before believing a gap under 2%.
# Duration (estimate): 60 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-dbf16
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,concurrent4_code_equal
